TriXium PCIe drivers

  trixium.ko    /dev/trixiumN: BAR0 (CSRs, the HBM loader) and the DMA rings.
  liteuart.ko  /dev/ttyLXUN: the firmware console over PCIe (the crossover UART).

The headers next to the sources (csr.h, soc.h, mem.h, flags.h, config.h) are generated per
SoC build - they must come from the build whose bitstream is on the card: the build scripts
generate them (--driver) in build/<name>/driver/kernel/, and the bring-up scripts copy them
here.

  make                 build both modules
  sudo ./init.sh       insmod both and make the device nodes world-writable
  make install         copy them to /lib/modules/.../extra + modules-load.d + a udev rule
  sudo rmmod trixium liteuart

Secure Boot refuses unsigned modules ("Lockdown: insmod: unsigned module loading is
restricted"); disable it in the BIOS.
